schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: Identity Verification in Web3
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: concept
  summary: >-
    Explains wallet-based identity verification as proving attributes about
    yourself (age, membership, location) without handing over documents to
    every counterparty, using zero-knowledge proofs and wallet-held
    credentials, framed for community members considering web3 grants,
    DAOs, or reputation-building in a Somaliland/East Africa context.
  audience: >-
    community members and stewards new to web3, evaluating whether/how to
    engage with verification-gated programs
  known_tensions:
    - >-
      access-to-verification-gated-opportunities-vs-privacy-cost-of-any-identity-linkage
  related_concepts:
    - zero-knowledge-proof-selective-disclosure
    - verifiable-credential-wallet-held-attestation
  related_resources: []
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/identity-verification.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  notes: >-
    assessed-but-excluded: the article has no References/sources section (its
    frontmatter sources: [] is empty) and names no specific verification
    protocol, product, or platform, so no resource object was created — the
    content is purely conceptual/explanatory. No public person-nodes or
    location-specific individual data were created; the Somaliland/Sarreya
    programs reference is kept general (audience framing only, no named
    individuals).
